-- title:
--   Tame vertex stabilisers for the away-unit groups Γ₂
-- statement:
--   The data are those of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd frame on the $q$-side, which are listed here group by group.
--
--   Arithmetic data. A positive squarefree integer $N$, two primes $q,q'$ with $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$, $q'\neq q$ and $5\le q$, $5\le q'$, and a positive integer $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$. A valuation subring $A_2$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ with `A₂.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A_2$; the hypothesis `hiso₂` records that the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ acts isometrically for the valuation of $A_2$; and a height-one prime $v_2$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q\in v_2$.
--
--   Definite side. Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt q'` for $B_1=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ every nonzero element of $B_1\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $q'\in v$. Further, $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules $\Lambda_1,R_1$ of $B_1$ with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) and $R_1\le\Lambda_1$; a finite-idelic unit $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ q`; the hypotheses that `meetOrder R₁ n₁` $=R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nq$ (`hS₁`), that it is normalised by $n_1$ (`hnorm₁`), and that the shift by $n_1$ on the class set of its finite-idelic stabiliser is an involution (`hsq₁`); finiteness of the relevant class sets; and `hlaws₁ : ClassSetHeckeLaws N q Λ₁ R₁ n₁`, the four-clause package asserting commutativity of the edge Hecke matrices, commutativity of the vertex Hecke matrices, compatibility of the degeneracy maps with Hecke operators away from $q$, and preservation of the joint kernel of the degeneracy maps.
--
--   Indefinite side and moduli in characteristic zero. Rationals $a,b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'` ($0<a$ or $0<b$, and $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is a division algebra exactly at the primes containing $q$ or $q'$), a maximal order $\Lambda$ in $B$; a field $Fbar$ that is a curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and essentially of finite type over it; a scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ (the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}$ away from $D$), a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar s$ of that base, and an assignment `pt` of $X$-points to fake elliptic curves for $\Lambda$ of level $N$, subject to the four coarse-moduli clauses `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, and surjectivity and injectivity on geometric points up to isomorphism); a curve model $\mathfrak{M}$ of $Fbar$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak{M}}$ onto the fibre product of $\pi_X$ and $\bar s$ compatible with the structural maps; a semilinear Galois action `gal`; tower data $\mathbb{T}$ for the primes away from $q,q'$ with actions `galT`, involutions $W$, $WT$; and a witness `tw : ModuliTowerWitnessD Λ N q q' D Fbar X πX sbar pt 𝔐 e𝔐 gal 𝕋 galT W WT` tying the places of $Fbar$ and of the tower fields to fake elliptic curves with and without extra level.
--
--   Local data at $q$. Writing $C=$ [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₂`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13) for the topological closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside the completion $A_2.\mathrm{valuation.Completion}$: an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota_2:B_1\to M_2(C)$, the induced homomorphism $\rho_2:B_1^{\times}\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(C)$ (with $h\rho_2$ saying $\rho_2$ is the class of $\iota_2$), a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi_2$ whose image in the completion is $q$, and a domain hypothesis on the associated ring of holomorphic functions. Elements $s_2(\ell)\in B_1^{\times}$ and finite ideles $sf_2(\ell)$ indexed by the primes $\ell\neq q,q'$, subject to `hs₂` (four clauses per $\ell$): away from $q$ the local component of $sf_2(\ell)$ is $s_2(\ell)\otimes 1$, at the primes over $q$ it is $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_2(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_2(\ell))=\ell$. Subgroups $\Gamma_2$ of $B_1^{\times}$ indexed by `HeckeTower.Obj q q'` with: $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ consisting of those $x$ lying in `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v₂` (the intersection, over height-one primes $w\neq v_2$, of the preimages under localisation at $w$ of the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R_1$ at $w$) for which $\mathrm{padicValRat}\ q(\mathrm{nrd}\ x)$ is even, and $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{some}\ \ell)=\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})\cap s_2(\ell)\,\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})\,s_2(\ell)^{-1}$. Atkin–Lehner-type elements $w_2$, $\bar w_2$ indexed by the same type, with `hw₂` requiring $w_2$ to lie in the corresponding away-unit groups and to have reduced norm $q$, and `hwbar₂` requiring $\bar w_2$ to have reduced norm $q'$, to localise into the local unit boxes at the primes different from $v_2$ not containing $q'$, and to normalise the local boxes of $R_1$ (respectively of `meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)`) and of $\Lambda_1$ at the primes different from $v_2$. A homomorphism $dIso_2$ from the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ to the isometric automorphisms of the completion realising the Galois action, and a quadratic character $\chi$ of that decomposition subgroup which is trivial on inertia, nontrivial on any Frobenius at $q$, and whose kernel consists of the elements fixing the elements $x$ of the residue field of $A_2$ with $x^{q^2}=x$.
--
--   Integral data. A domain $\mathcal{O}_0$ of characteristic zero that is a discrete valuation ring with irreducible $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, residue field of cardinality $q$, with $(q)=(\pi)$, having $C$ as fraction field and with $N$ invertible; a domain $Onr$ of characteristic zero over $\mathcal{O}_0$ with an $\mathcal{O}_0$-automorphism $Fr$, complete and with maximal ideal generated by $\pi$, every element integral over $\mathcal{O}_0$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{q}$ modulo $\pi$; a homomorphism $vdet$ from $\mathrm{GL}_2(C)$ to $\mathbb{Z}$ characterised by `hvdet` as the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant; a ring map $\psi_0:Onr\to A_2.\mathrm{valuation.Completion}$ with values of valuation at most $1$ and compatible with $\mathcal{O}_0$; the identification of $\pi$ with $\varpi_2$; the description of $\mathcal{O}_0$ inside $C$ as the elements of valuation at most $1$; and the rank-one condition `hrk`.
--
--   Moduli over $\mathcal{O}_0$ and the uniformisation datum. An integral scheme $\mathcal{X}_0$ with a flat, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact morphism $f_0$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$ and a point assignment $pt_0$ making it a coarse moduli space `IsCoarseModuli Λ N 𝒳₀ f₀ pt₀` for fake elliptic curves of level $N$; schemes $\mathcal{Y}_0(\ell)$ with morphisms $g_0(\ell)$ and assignments $ptT_0(\ell)$ that are coarse moduli spaces for fake elliptic curves with extra $\ell$-level; two degeneracy morphisms $d_{00}(\ell),d_{10}(\ell):\mathcal{Y}_0(\ell)\to\mathcal{X}_0$ over $\mathcal{O}_0$ inducing, on points, forgetting the extra level and dividing by it; and endomorphisms $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal{X}_0$ over $\mathcal{O}_0$ inducing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $q$ and at $q'$. Finally, families of maps $\Theta$ and $\Theta_T(\ell)$ from the functor $B\mapsto (Onr\to_{\mathcal{O}_0}B)\times \mathrm{Omega}(B)$ on $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent to the nilpotent points of $f_0$, respectively of $g_0(\ell)$, together with the hypothesis `hCD` (twelve clauses, summarised here): naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta_T(\ell)$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action of the elements of `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v₂` and of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ under that of the intersection of this group with its conjugate by $s_2(\ell)$; over every algebraically closed $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, surjectivity of $\Theta$ and of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ at a fixed $Onr$-component and the identification of their fibres with the orbits of those groups; the corresponding universal properties of the nilpotent points of $f_0$ and of $g_0(\ell)$ among functors so invariant; compatibility of $d_{00}(\ell)$ with $\Theta_T(\ell)$ and $\Theta$, and of $d_{10}(\ell)$ with the twisted action of $s_2(\ell)$; and the description of $ar$ by the Frobenius twist $Fr$ on the $Onr$-component and of $arbar$ by the twisted action of $\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})$.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of the following two assertions, both concerning the vertices of the lattice tree [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪₀ C`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349), that is, the homothety classes of full $\mathcal{O}_0$-lattices in $C^2$.
--
--   First: for every vertex $v$, the value under the valuation of $A_2.\mathrm{valuation.Completion}$ of the image of the natural number $\mathrm{Nat.card}\{g\in \mathrm{PGL}_2(C) : g\in \rho_2(\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none}))\ \text{and}\ g\cdot v=v\}$ equals $1$.
--
--   Second: for every prime $\ell$ away from $q$ and $q'$ and every vertex $v$, the value under that valuation of the image of $\mathrm{Nat.card}\{g\in \mathrm{PGL}_2(C) : g\in \rho_2(\Gamma_2(\mathrm{some}\ \ell))\ \text{and}\ g\cdot v=v\}$ equals $1$.
--
--   Since $\mathrm{Nat.card}$ vanishes on infinite types and the valuation of $0$ is not $1$, each assertion entails both that the stabiliser in question is finite and that its order is a unit for the valuation, hence prime to the residue characteristic $q$.
--
--   This is the tameness input on the $q$-side of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation: the vertex stabilisers of the image of the away-unit groups $\Gamma_2$ in $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ acting on the tree have order prime to $q$, the classical reason being that finite subgroups of the unit group of a definite rational quaternion algebra modulo scalars have order dividing $24$. It is stated in the full frame of that construction and is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_mumfordEmbedding_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_zero_one_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_mumfordEmbedding_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_zero_one_of_two_mul_dvd), where the absence of wild stabilisers is what allows the Mumford-curve description of the quotient; the proof goes through [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_not_dvd_natCard_of_mumfordSideFrame`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_not_dvd_natCard_of_mumfordSideFrame).
